<section class="section timing-section">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <div class="timing-intro fade-up">
      <div class="section-label">Your Site Is Working Against You</div>
      <h2>Your Agency Grew. Your Website Is Still Stuck in Year One.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="accordion fade-up">
      <div class="accordion-item open">
        <button class="accordion-trigger" aria-expanded="true">
          <span>The AMS Template Problem</span>
          <svg class="accordion-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="accordion-content">
          <p>You&rsquo;ve added producers, expanded your book, and built a real operation. But if your website still looks like it did three years ago (or worse, it came from the template your AMS vendor handed you), ithanded you. it&rsquo;s notrsquo;s not keeping up with the agency you&rsquo;ve become.</p>
          <p>HawkSoft, Applied, Vertafore. They&rsquo;re great for running your book. They&rsquo;re not web design companies, and the sites they provide look exactly like what they are: placeholders with your logo on them. Same layout. Same stock photos. Same generic &ldquo;get a quote&rdquo; button that nobody clicks. Meanwhile, the agency down the street with a real site is getting the call.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="accordion-item">
        <button class="accordion-trigger" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>What Real Agency Sites Do</span>
          <svg class="accordion-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="accordion-content">
          <p>A real agency website shows up in the local map pack when someone searches &ldquo;insurance agency near me.&rdquo; It loads in under two seconds on a phone. It has a clear call-to-action above the fold, real photos of your team, carrier logos that build trust, and client reviews that close the deal before you ever pick up the phone.</p>
          <p>It&rsquo;s not a brochure: itbrochure. it&rsquo;s a toolrsquo;s a tool that works for you around the clock. Every page has a job. Every element earns its place. And when a prospect lands on it, they don&rsquo;t bounce to the next agency. They call you.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="accordion-item">
        <button class="accordion-trigger" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>The Timing Window</span>
          <svg class="accordion-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="accordion-content">
          <p>A proper website rebuild takes 8&ndash;12 weeks. If your peak season starts in September, that puts Q2 as the last comfortable window to start. Every week you wait compresses the timeline and raises the cost.</p>
          <p><span class="hl">Getting your grade now gives you time to fix it, not scramble.</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script is:inline>
  document.querySelectorAll('.accordion-trigger').forEach(trigger => {
    trigger.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const item = trigger.parentElement;
      const isOpen = item.classList.contains('open');

      // Close all items
      document.querySelectorAll('.accordion-item').forEach(i => {
        i.classList.remove('open');
        i.querySelector('.accordion-trigger').setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
      });

      // Open clicked item if it was closed
      if (!isOpen) {
        item.classList.add('open');
        trigger.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
      }
    });
  });
</script>

<style>
  .timing-section {
    background: var(--white);
  }

  .timing-intro {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto 40px;
  }

  .accordion {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .accordion-item {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e5ea;
  }

  .accordion-item:first-child {
    border-top: 1px solid #e2e5ea;
  }

  .accordion-trigger {
    width: 100%;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 20px 0;
    background: none;
    border: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-family: inherit;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .accordion-trigger span {
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--charcoal);
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .accordion-trigger:hover span {
    color: var(--orange);
  }

  .accordion-chevron {
    color: var(--text-light);
    transition: transform 0.3s;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .accordion-item.open .accordion-chevron {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }

  .accordion-item.open .accordion-trigger span {
    color: var(--orange);
  }

  .accordion-content {
    max-height: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: max-height 0.3s ease, padding 0.3s ease;
    padding: 0 0;
  }

  .accordion-item.open .accordion-content {
    max-height: 500px;
    padding: 0 0 24px;
  }

  .accordion-content p {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-light);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .accordion-content p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>
